<%--
Form_Field

Wrapper component that provides consistent label, help text, and error display for form widgets.

$label - Label text, plain string (use <Slot:label> for markup) [optional]
$required - Boolean - if true, shows red asterisk next to label
$help - Help text to display below the field

<Slot:label> - label override; WINS over $label when present (dual-channel, D2)
widget - the form input as loose content, OR inside <Slot:body> when <Slot:label> is used

Title/label channel rule: plain text -> $label arg; ANY markup/icon/nesting -> <Slot:label>.
HTML placed inside the $label string is a defect (it now renders escaped).

SLOT RULE (jqhtml): with <Slot:label>, the input MUST move into <Slot:body>
(the parser forbids loose content beside a named slot):
<Form_Field><Slot:label><i class="bi bi-star"></i> Rating</Slot:label>
    <Slot:body><Text_Input $name="rating" /></Slot:body></Form_Field>

NOTE: $name goes on the INPUT component, not on Form_Field:
<Form_Field $label="Email Address" $required=true>
    <Text_Input $name="email" $placeholder="user@example.com" />
</Form_Field>

The input component sets data-name on itself, and Form_Field reads it
for error display integration.
--%>
<Define:Form_Field extends="Form_Field_Abstract" tag="div" class="form-group mb-3">

    <% const _has_label_slot = !!(this.args._slots && this.args._slots.label); %>
    <% if (_has_label_slot || this.args.label) { %>
        <label class="form-label" $sid="form_label">
            <% if (_has_label_slot) { %>
                <%= content('label') %>
            <% } else { %>
                <%= this.args.label %>
            <% } %>
            <% if (this.args.required) { %>
                <span class="text-danger">*</span>
            <% } %>
        </label>
    <% } %>

    <div class="<%= this.has_error() ? 'is-invalid' : '' %>">
        <% if (this.args._slots && this.args._slots.body) { %>
            <%= content('body') %>
        <% } else { %>
            <%= content() %>
        <% } %>
    </div>

    <% if (this.has_error()) { %>
        <div class="invalid-feedback d-block">
            <%= this.get_error() %>
        </div>
    <% } %>

    <% if (this.args.help) { %>
        <small class="form-text text-muted d-block mt-1">
            <%= this.args.help %>
        </small>
    <% } %>

</Define:Form_Field>
